trial Engineering\nMechanical and Aerospace Engineering\nCertificate Programs\nUndergraduate Programs\nMaster's Programs\nDoctorate Programs\nFive Year Joint BS/MS Program\nREU Program in Coastal Infrastructure Resilience Research (Summer)\n$sLabel\nHome\nAcademics\nAll Programs\nDoctorate Programs\nAAA\nDoctorate Programs\nCertificate Programs\nUndergraduate Programs\nMaster's Programs\nDoctorate Programs\nFive Year Joint BS/MS Program\nREU Program in Coastal Infrastructure Resilience Research (Summer)\nGET STARTED\n1\nRequest Info\n2\nVisit\n3\nApply\nPursue a PhD engineering degree in Miami and unravel the unknown\u2026.\nThe College of Engineering at the University of Miami offers a range of doctoral programs. Students can pursue PhD degrees with a single faculty member, or collaboratively in interdisciplinary projects with multiple faculty investigators. The College is engaged in addressing challenging problems, and organized in six strategic areas to solve some of the most pressing societal problems.\nIf selected for admission through a competitive process, all doctoral students receive financial assistance including a monthly stipend and a full tuition waiver.\nThe College of Engineering has six comprehensive departments, and each of them offer PhD Programs:\nBiomedical Engineering\nMedical Physics\nCivil and Architectural Engineering\nChemical, Environmental and Materials Engineering\nElectrical and Computer Engineering\nIndustrial Engineering\nMechanical and Aerospace Engineering\nPhD Research Advisors\nPotential applicants are strongly encouraged to contact faculty experts in their field of expertise by searching through our database of faculty experts. You can also choose earn a PhD degree in Engineering with Advisors from other highly ranked programs at other departments and schools in the University \u2013 such as the Bascom Palmer School of Opthalmology, Sylvester Comprehensive Cancer Center, Miami Project, Rosenstiel School of Marine and Atmospheric Sciences, and others.\nPriority Application Deadline: December 1\nThe University of Miami College of Engineering admits PhD students only for entry for the Fall semester. The application for admission with supporting documents should be completed before the priority admission deadline of December 1 (international applicants are highly encouraged to submit their completed applications as early as possible in order to ensure ample time for the student visa process if accepted for admission).\nPhD Admissions: Apply Today\nRequest Info\nTop\nUniversity of Miami\nCoral Gables, FL 33124\n305-284-2211\nCollege of Engineering\n1251 Memorial Drive, McArthur Engineering Building\nCoral Gables,\nFL\n33146\n(305) 284-2404\n(305) 284-2404\nResources\nAbout UM\nmyUM\nCaneLink\nAcademic Calendar\nCanvas/Blackboard\nUM Network\nAlumni & Friends\nMedical Center\nHurricane Sports\nCareers\nSupport COE\nGive to COE\nWays to Give\nVisit\nCampus Map\nParking & Transportation\nConnect\nsocial-instagram\nsocial-linkedin\nsocial-twitter\nsocial-facebook\nCopyright: 2026 University of Miami. All Rights Reserved.\nEmergency Information\nPrivacy Statement & Legal Notices\nIndividuals with disabilities who experience any technology-based barriers accessing University websites can submit details to our online form.", "links": [["Skip to Content", "https://www.coe.miami.edu/academics/programs/doctorate-programs/index.html#accessibility-content"], ["Skip to Search", "https://www.coe.miami.edu/academics/programs/doctorate-programs/index.html#default-js-input"], ["Skip to footer", "https://www.coe.miami.edu/academics/programs/doctorate-programs/index.html#global_footer"], ["Office of Disability Services", "https://camnercenter.miami.edu/disability-services/index.html"], ["Request Assistance", "https://camnercenter.miami.edu/disability-services/request-services/index.html"], ["Default", "https://www.coe.miami.edu/academics/programs/doctorate-programs/index.html"], ["High Contrast", "https://cdn.miami